In C++, data types define the type of data a variable can store. Common data types include int, float, char, and double. A variable stores data, and a constant stores fixed data. Example:
int age = 20;
const float pi = 3.14;
Here, age is a variable and pi is a constant.

Variables in C++ are declared by specifying the data type followed by the variable name. Constants are declared using the const keyword. Example:
double salary = 45000.50;
const int MAX = 100;
The value of MAX cannot be changed during program execution.

C++ में data types यह बताते हैं कि variable किस type का data store करेगा। Example: int, float, char. Variable change हो सकता है, लेकिन constant fixed होता है। Example:
int marks = 90;
const int passMarks = 40;
यहाँ marks variable है और passMarks constant है।

